# A liveness ping from a gizmo.
#
# A second root namespace, and its whole reason for existing is that it
# refers to the same standard timestamp `kitbag` does. Two namespaces
# sharing a dependency is the ordinary case, and it is the one that
# forces a build to decide who generates the shared type -- generate it
# from both and two rules produce one file, which Ninja refuses outright.
#
# Only the Ninja cell builds this. The other cells target the kitbag
# namespace directly and never see it.

uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 at
# When the ping was sent, on the network-synchronised timebase.

uint16 sequence
# Increments once per ping, wrapping. A receiver uses the gaps to
# estimate loss.

@sealed
